35
00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:03.769
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): I'm a maintainer of hyperlogger cacti. I've been involved with the community for many happy years now.

36
00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:11.600
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): And I reached out to share some of our findings on AI

37
00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:20.839
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): LLMs, or LLMs that are a subset of research on AI that could be useful for… not only for Cacti, but for our projects.

38
00:04:21.089 --> 00:04:25.109
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Am I able to share my screen? I prepared a short presentation.

39
00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:25.959
Jessica Gonzalez (The Linux Foundation): Yeah, for sure.

40
00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:27.760
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Couple ideas will.

41
00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:28.130
Jessica Gonzalez (The Linux Foundation): governing.

42
00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:28.760
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): principle.

43
00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.130
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Thank you.

44
00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.269
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Thank you. So… So let's go ahead.

45
00:04:43.910 --> 00:05:01.759
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): The motivation for this initiative is very simple. We've noticed that a larger share of contributions to Cacti seem to be AI-assisted or LM assisted, and this trend seems to be very present in the industry and even academia.

46
00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:11.120
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): So, it would be a good idea to explore how these tools can assist our projects and help us

47
00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:15.530
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Review contributions in a more… impartial way.

48
00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:22.909
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Secondly, LLMs are being used by black hat hackers and other threat actors to

49
00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:31.209
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Exploit vulnerabilities at scale in different open source projects, and not only open source projects, but

50
00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:43.880
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): deployed industry projects, so… This is a threat that's relatively new, but emerging in a very… large-scale capacity.

51
00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.610
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): So, the idea would be to…

52
00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:58.020
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): understand the risks that are behind LLMs used for black hacking, black hat hacking, and take some countermeasures to it.

53
00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:05.650
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): And finally, we… we searched, on the Linux, on Linux Foundation for…

54
00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:11.259
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): AI-specific guidelines, there are a few pointers, and thanks, Ryan, for pointing it out.

55
00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:18.029
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): But non-specific for projects like hyperlogger cacti, so we want to take a first shot at this.

56
00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:29.479
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): So we came with this pull request, which contains several items. One of them is this document AI guidelines, and here are the core principles summarized.

57
00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:35.809
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): One of the most important ones, in my opinion, it's the human responsibility core principle, which means that

58
00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:46.590
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): the person that wrote a piece of code, being LLM-assisted or not, owns the code. It's, his or their responsibility to maintain it.

59
00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:55.020
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Also, the AI output, even if one instructs an LLM to review code, does not mean that a code review has been done, so…

60
00:06:55.220 --> 00:07:01.829
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Our definition of code review is that it is done by a human, even if the AI assists on the process.

61
00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:08.180
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Then, another core principle is disclosure, so this is,

62
00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:23.010
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): This is a prominent challenge nowadays, because many of the contributions are being done without any disclosure, and that could add some risks, and we can discuss them. But the core idea here is that when we use LRMs.

63
00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:30.290
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): We are incentivized, or not forbidden, at the very least, to use them, but we need to disclose which one did we use and how.

64
00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.970
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Preferentially.

65
00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.339
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Then, this is more of a legal…

66
00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:56.420
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): points, and I'm not… I'm not a legal expert or a lawyer, so I would appreciate your input, but we should ensure that the LLM tool used for adding code, or for contributing to any of our projects, is compatible with the generic license that we were using.

67
00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:12.210
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): And this can be tricky, because as LLMs are trained on publicly available data, including open source projects, the output of an LLM for a specific question might be taken from a project with a different license, let's say GLP2.

68
00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.630
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): a GPL tool.

69
00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:22.740
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): And… If this is the case, this particular license has a problem, because it requires

70
00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:30.300
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): That, projects that use the code from this license to have the same license, which would

71
00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:34.640
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Put, potentially, our project in a legal problem.

72
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:36.880
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): And finally.

73
00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:51.610
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): AI is used as a development tool, not as a tool to replace human judgment. So, it cannot be listed as an author, but it can be listed, and it should be listed as a helper, as an assister. It cannot approve PRs, it cannot

74
00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:57.360
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): sign the DCO or make governance decisions. Those are deferred to the maintainers and contributors of the project.

75
00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:04.640
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): So, those are the core principles that are on this PR that we've shared.

76
00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:10.269
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): The PR is… and the specific commit with the guidelines is there.

77
00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:27.370
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): The PR is also listed here. We also add a few more things to Cacti as a proof of concept. Not only the AI guidelines, but also a couple skills, agent workflows, instructions. We also use an LLM to summarize the repository conventions.

78
00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:36.220
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): to… to assist contributors and maintainers to use these tools effectively. Again, this is a very new technology, and this,

79
00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:37.970
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): an initial effort.

80
00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.509
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): So we are also learning in the process.

81
00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.679
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): So if I had to create a…

82
00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:48.710
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): a final commit for these guidelines already following the guidelines, I would do something like this.

83
00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:53.229
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): I also, used Cloud Opus to help me

84
00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.890
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): Put together bullet points for this presentation.

85
00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:09.070
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): So finally, if we could provide a minimal set of recommendations for your consideration, we would endorse

86
00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:28.019
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): responsible AI use defensive here in terms of security to address the multiple security vulnerabilities across the different hyperlogger projects, and also the creation and maintenance of these guidelines documents, not only for the case of hyperlogger cacti, but

87
00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:33.730
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): But all the… open source projects that the Linux Foundation oversees.

88
00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:44.099
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): And this concludes my presentation. Thank you for your attention. I'm happy to discuss any of these items, either here or…

89
00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:45.720
Rafael  Belchior (INESC-ID): In our Discord.

